Sometimes you need to work with a callback style function from 3rd party library or an existing one in your codebase. Something like this.

const generateToken = (callback) => {

... // some async process ... callback(token) // success case ... callback(null, error) // failure case }

You will have a problem if you want to use it in the async function. You could turn the function into also async function, not taking the callback function but most of the time you have no control or you don’t want to touch it. This is an easy solution for this kind of situation and I will describe it as much as short and simple.

You can create a wrapper function that calls the original function inside and returns a Promise.

const generateTokenWrapper = () =>

new Promise((resolve, reject) => {

generateToken((token, error) => {

if (error) {

reject(error)

} else {

resolve(token)

}

})

})

And you can use it like this in your async function.

try {

const token = await generateTokenWrapper()

console.log({ token })

} catch (error) {

console.error({ error })

}

That’s it. I hope it works in your situation.

Lastly, here’s a working example. Enjoy!

AAA(Arrange-Act-Assert) Pattern於撰寫測試時經常出現，在寫一個測試案例需要準備測試所需的環境和測試資料，也就是Arrange階段。在此階段經常會需要建立待測物件所需的dependency，如果每個測試案例都經常需要相同的物件，我們可以簡單地透過Factory Method Pattern來避免程式碼重複(DRY, Don’t Repeat Yourself)．如果參數需要做微調則可以利用OOP的Method Overload來達成，在有預設值的情況下想要微調特定參數，如IP位址、裝置名稱，如下所示：

public class DeviceTests {

... private DeviceInfo CreateDeviceInfo() {

return new DeviceInfo(Guid.NewGuid(), IP, NAME, STATE);

} private DeviceInfo CreateDeviceInfo(string ip) {

return new DeviceInfo(Guid.NewGuid(), ip, NAME, STATE);

} private DeviceInfo CreateDeviceInfo(string name) {

return new DeviceInfo(Guid.NewGuid(), IP, name, STATE);

}

}

這樣在Arrage階段建立新的DeviceInfo時可以直接呼叫CreateDeviceInfo()，除此之外，還可以避免將DeviceInfo定義為Field，將測試資料定義在Field不僅會導致日後測試難以維護，可讀性也相當差，且缺乏彈性．如果遇到上面情況需要微調就只能在Test Case中重新new新的DeviceInfo，使用Factory Method使得每個測試更加獨立，不共用Field，在Arrage階段呼叫Factory Method取得新的DeviceInfo還可以讓語意更加明確．

但是，可以看到此程式碼產生了Duplicated Code的情形，因為DeviceInfo是Data Object會有許多資料，測試時因情況需要，微調時就會出現多個函式之間有點像又有點不像的情況．要解決這個問題我們可以透過Builder Pattern來進行封裝，由於每個欄位都有預設值，因此我命名為DefaultBuilder，如下所示：

public class DefaultDeviceInfoBuilder {

private Guid id;

private string ip;

private string name;

private bool state; public DefaultDeviceInfoBuilder() {

id = Guid.NewGuid();

ip = "192.168.0.100";

name = "Default Name";

state = false;

} public DefaultDeviceInfoBuilder SetIp(string ip) {

this.ip = ip;

return this;

}



public DefaultDeviceInfoBuilder SetName(string name) {

this.name = name;

return this;

}



public DeviceInfo Build() {

return new DeviceInfo(id, ip, name, state);

}

} public class DeviceTests {

private DeviceInfo CreateDeviceInfo(string ip) {

return new DefaultDeviceInfoBuilder()

.SetIp(ip)

.Build();

}

}

這樣在建立DeviceInfo時可以避免不必要的重複，也不會對於DeviceInfo的constructor過度依賴，導致constructor改變時測試需要大量的修改，影響範圍太廣等問題．

如果DeviceInfo只在相同Test Class中使用，CreateDeviceInfo() Factory Method放在相同class中就夠了．但如果DeviceInfo也被其他幾個Test Class使用到，就不好在其他測試中也重新定義相同的Factory Method，因為也會違反DRY原則，因此必須將其獨立出Factory Class，如下所示：

public class DefaultDeviceInfoFactory {

public DeviceInfo Create() {

return new DefaultDeviceInfoBuilder().Build();

} public DeviceInfo Create(string ip) {

return new DefaultDeviceInfoBuilder()

.SetIp(ip)

.Build;

}

...

}

可以先定義多個Test Class都需要的Factory Method就好，如果只有一個Test Class需要使用，可以先定義在自己的類別中，等有重複情況時再抽取出來．

結論：測試也需要DRY，把Builder當作特殊微調使用，而Factory Class中的函式則是經常被使用的，可以讓測試更乾淨、更好維護．

參考：

[1] https://reflectoring.io/objectmother-fluent-builder/?fbclid=IwAR2iBT9QiHN0NERycV-2x-6a7PUomvkyBb-rySBFi99vxt0o5CTMbVv-Oqc

[2] https://www.amazon.com/Practical-Object-Oriented-Design-Ruby-Addison-Wesley/dp/0321721330

The pattern belongs to the behavioral category of the design patterns.

Idea

Provide a way to access the elements of an aggregate object sequentially without exposing its underlying representation.

Explanation

Wikipedia says:

In object-oriented programming, the iterator pattern is a design pattern in which an iterator is used to traverse a container and access the container’s elements. The iterator pattern decouples algorithms from containers; in some cases, algorithms are necessarily container-specific and thus cannot be decoupled.

In plain words:

Provide a way to access the elements of an aggregate object sequentially without exposing its underlying representation.

Class Diagram

The class diagram will be:

Example

The task:

Let’s extend configs class by adding implementation for the iteration logic.

Let’s implement the iterator interface:

public final class Configs implements Config, Iterator<Config> {

private int position = 0;

private final List<Config> configs = new LinkedList<>();



public void add(final Config config) {

configs.add(config);

}



public void remove(final Config config) {

configs.remove(config);

}



@Override

public int getId() {

int value = 0;

for (final var config : configs) {

value += config.getId();

}



return value;

}



@Override

public String getName() {

final var name = new StringBuilder();

for (final var config : configs) {

name.append(config.getName()).append(";");

}



name.deleteCharAt(name.indexOf(";"));

return name.toString();

}



@Override

public boolean hasNext() {

return position < configs.size() - 1;

}



@Override

public Config next() {

if (!hasNext()) {

throw new NoSuchElementException();

}



return configs.get(position++);

}

}

And then it can be used as:

final var configs = new Configs();

configs.add(new UserConfig(1001, "Name 1"));

configs.add(new UserConfig(1002, "Name 2"));

configs.add(new UserConfig(1003, "Name 3"));



var position = 1;

while (configs.hasNext()) {

final var config = configs.next();

assertEquals(1000 + position, config.getId());

assertEquals("Name " + position, config.getName());

position++;

}

More Examples

