So what have we’ve been learning thus far in our cohorts learning journey? To begin with one such example, we have recently gone over how to fetch information from an API public database. We were then tasked to create our own one page site, where we demonstrate our ability to complete such a task, where a user interacts with the page asynchronously. That is to say, without the need of say, refreshing the page. In my example, I created a sort of Pokemon card page (though it is sloppy to say so myself in terms of appearance.), where the user can easily shuffle the cards before them and a set of new cards appear.

